{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I sought the Lord and he heard my [Em]cry
[C]He answered me from the other [D]side
[G]Delivered me from [D/F#]all [Em]my fears
The [C]weight of the [G]world disap[D]pears
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G]Taste and [D]see that the Lord [Em]is good
[C]Blessed is the [G]one who [Am]stands in his blood
[G]Refuge [D]found in the shel[Em]ter of grace
[Am7]No matter [G]the price of [D]time or [G]space
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Those who look to him [D/F#]shine [Em]with light
Their [C]faces never see the night of [D]shame
[G]The poor man called and [D/F#]the [Em]Lord heard
[Am7]He saved him from every trouble [D]found
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G]Taste and [D]see that the Lord [Em]is good
[C]Blessed is the [G]one who [Am7]stands in his blood
[G]Refuge [D]found in the shel[Em]ter of grace
